sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Client process
  participant CK as Client kernel
  participant SK as Server kernel
  participant S as Server process
  S->>SK: socket(), bind(:9000), listen(backlog)
  Note over SK: listening socket: SYN queue + accept queue
  C->>CK: socket(), connect(server:9000)
  CK->>SK: SYN
  SK-->>CK: SYN-ACK
  CK->>SK: ACK
  Note over SK: connection complete, placed on accept queue
  S->>SK: accept()
  SK-->>S: new connected fd (listening fd unchanged)
  C->>CK: send(44 bytes)
  CK->>SK: segments (the boundaries are TCP's choice, not yours)
  S->>SK: recv(buf, 4096)
  SK-->>S: returns 1..44 bytes (any prefix!)
  C->>CK: close()
  CK->>SK: FIN
  S->>SK: recv() returns 0 (EOF)
